# Phase 12 (Plan 12-08) — Chrome extension stable-ID keypair.
#
# The PRIVATE key (RSA PEM) is generated locally by the operator, kept
# OUTSIDE git (canonical location: ~/.config/xbrain/secrets/chrome-ext-key.pem),
# and ONLY needed when publishing to Chrome Web Store later (used as the
# "upload key" that binds the Store listing to the dev identity).
#
# For day-to-day unpacked installs the base64-encoded PUBLIC key embedded
# in manifest.json is sufficient — the private PEM is NOT required at
# runtime.
#
# Defense-in-depth: the repo root .gitignore already excludes *.pem, but
# we duplicate the rule here so a future copy/move that drops the parent
# .gitignore doesn't silently expose the key.
chrome_ext_private.pem
chrome_ext_private_*.pem
chrome-ext-key.pem
*.pem
*.key
